{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 13, :comments ["<b>I am the El of Bethel</b>. Jacob tells his wives everything that the angel of Elohim said to him in the dream, for it is all an appeasement of them so that they will go with him. But what he tells them is not one dream, for the statement \"Lift now your eyes and see all the goats\" (Genesis 31:12) was while he was tending Laban's flock, at the time the sheep mated, in one of the first years; and the statement \"I am the El of Bethel\" was afterward, at the time of the journey, for after He said to him \"Arise, go out from this land\" (Genesis 31:13), he no longer lingered in Haran to tend Laban's sheep further and have the he-goats mount the flock and give birth to speckled and spotted ones. Rather, on the morning after the dream he sent for Rachel and for Leah and told them his dream, and they set out. And the meaning of \"I am the El of Bethel\": Rashi (Rashi on Genesis 31:13) explains that the letter ה is superfluous, and it is like \"I am El Bethel,\" similar to \"to the land of Canaan\" (Numbers 34:2). And the masters of the language (Ibn Ezra and Radak) set it as \"I am the El, El of Bethel,\" and likewise \"and the tree of knowledge of good and evil\" (Genesis 2:9), \"the twisted chains of gold\" (Exodus 39:17), and the angel speaks in the language of the One who sent him. And by way of truth, this angel says \"I am the El of Bethel,\" and likewise \"and he called the place El Bethel\" (Genesis 35:7), as it says \"Zion, the Holy One of Israel\" (Isaiah 60:14). And Jonathan ben Uziel said (there, 6:3), \"The Holy One from on high, whose name is exalted, the House of His Shekhinah,\" and he is the redeeming angel (Genesis 48:16), and likewise \"in all My house he is trusted\" (Numbers 12:7), and the discerning will understand." "And the meaning of <b>where you anointed a pillar, where you vowed a vow to Me there</b>: for you vowed to be a servant to HaShem, the unified One, in the chosen land, and for the stone to be for you a house of Elohim, and to bring forth your tithes there, and if you delay your vows further, Elohim will again be angered at your voice."], :book :genesis, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 31, :notes {0 "The Aramaic citation from Targum Jonathan corresponds to Genesis 28:17, not 6:3 as written in the Hebrew text; the reference has been translated as printed."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:37:47.480916721Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}